    "content": "# Intent routing with hand-off to a specialist agent.\n# Alternate paths (routing to a different specialist, or escalating\n# to a human) would be separate Sessions following the same pattern —\n# this is the v0.1 way to handle bifurcations.\n\nsession: Intent routing — damaged item → refund\ndescription: >\n  User reports a damaged item. Triage detects refund intent,\n  hands off to Refunds Agent who verifies and processes the return.\nbehaviors:\n  # ── Triage ──\n  - actor: user\n    action: says\n    content: \"I received a damaged item, I want my money back. Order #8291.\"\n    capture:\n      orderId: \"8291\"\n\n  - actor: assistant\n    action: clarifies\n    content: \"I understand — you want to return order #8291 because it arrived damaged. Let me connect you with our refunds specialist.\"\n    evaluations:\n      - type: llm_judge\n        criteria: |\n          1. Identifies the request as a refund, not a general inquiry\n          2. References the order number #8291\n          3. States they are routing to the refunds specialist specifically\n\n  # ── Hand-off ──\n  - actor: assistant\n    action: hands_off\n    target: Refunds Agent\n    content: \"Refund request: order #8291, reason: damaged\"\n    evaluations:\n      - type: llm_judge\n        criteria: |\n          1. Hands off to Refunds Agent — not Orders, not Human\n          2. Passes both order number and reason in the hand-off context\n\n  # ── Specialist resolves ──\n  - actor: assistant\n    action: greets\n    content: \"Hi, I'm the refunds specialist. I've pulled up order #8291 — confirmed it was delivered damaged. Let me process your return now.\"\n    evaluations:\n      - type: llm_judge\n        criteria: |\n          1. Introduces as refunds specialist (new agent identity)\n          2. Confirms the damage and order number\n          3. Takes ownership of the resolution\n\n  - actor: assistant\n    action: calls\n    target: Refunds API\n    with:\n      orderId: \"{{orderId}}\"\n      reason: \"damaged\"\n\n  - actor: tool\n    action: responds\n    target: Refunds API\n    content:\n      refundId: \"R-5512\"\n      amount: 47.50\n      status: \"approved\"\n\n  - actor: assistant\n    action: informs\n    content: \"Refund of €47.50 approved, Franco. You'll receive it in 3-5 days. Reference: R-5512.\"\n    capture:\n      refundId: \"R-5512\"\n    evaluations:\n      - type: contains\n        value: \"R-5512\"\n      - type: llm_judge\n        criteria: |\n          1. States the refund amount and timeline clearly\n          2. Provides the refund reference R-5512\n          3. Reassuring tone, no upsells\n\n# ── Chain: the full trace across the hand-off boundary ──\nevaluations:\n  - type: sequence\n    order:\n      - { actor: assistant, action: clarifies }\n      - { actor: assistant, action: hands_off, target: \"Refunds Agent\" }\n      - { actor: assistant, action: greets }\n      - { actor: assistant, action: calls, target: \"Refunds API\" }\n      - { actor: assistant, action: informs }\n\n  # Routing guards: this path must NOT have gone elsewhere\n  - type: never\n    match: { actor: assistant, action: hands_off, target: \"Human Agent\" }\n\n  # The refund ID must be consistent everywhere it appears\n  - type: variable_consistency\n    variable: refundId\n\n# Alternate paths (not shown — each would be its own Session):\n#   - \"Where is my order?\" → hands_off to Orders Agent → order lookup\n#   - \"My account was hacked!\" → hands_off to Human Agent → no automation"
